WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.460
Larry P. Arnn:
The government is the necessary solution to

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.140
a problem and that is us.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:15.890
Lord knows what we might do without laws,
but there's a problem with government, that's

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.480
us too.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.760
First of all the name means something cool.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.010
It means to set a thing up firmly in place.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.510
It's actually like the word [inaudible 00:29].

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.270
Just think of this particular problem.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.139
If you're going to have more than one person
make the law, you're going to have to have

00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:44.579
a constitution to describe how that's done
or else, you're going to have wars all the

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:47.139
time about who gets to make the law.

00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:54.870
The constitution is an attempt to organize
a form of government that is as close as possible

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:59.709
to what human beings are like and what they
need.

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:05.750
What they're like is that they need and they
naturally make laws and what they need is

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:12.500
those laws to be consistently fair and protect
them and also restrain them from harming one

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.460
another.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:21.050
Since it's true that both the things that
needs protecting and the danger to it is the

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:29.200
same thing, then you have to have some method
of both assembling and granting power and

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.680
of restraining power.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.390
Our constitution is the best at that in all
of history and the explanations of it by the

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:42.950
people who wrote it are the most profound
explanations of that kind in all of human

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.810
history.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.159
Is self government possible?

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:56.590
All of human history, all the kings, and monarchs,
and aristocracy of history had thought, "No.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.320
It can't be done."

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.360
Aristotle himself is very skeptical.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:07.740
He's not opposed, but he's skeptical about
democracy, the rule of the many.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:13.030
The founders are aware this is a very hard
thing to do.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:20.700
Indeed, never done in history for a long time
before.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.970
The constitution has to be respected.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:29.430
It's the law that gives the process by which
we make all the other laws.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:37.359
It is the only law really ever passed directly
by the people of the United States.

00:02:37.359 --> 00:02:44.549
The people picked the constitution and if
you think as I think that no human being has

00:02:44.549 --> 00:02:50.200
the right by nature to govern any other human
being without a consent of the governed, then

00:02:50.200 --> 00:03:00.550
of course you have to think that the majority
has to approve the government all the time.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:05.169
You don't want the majority tampering with
the constitution all the time and so they

00:03:05.169 --> 00:03:12.779
invented a process for the people to pass
the constitution more less directly and then

00:03:12.779 --> 00:03:23.010
that process passed away and doesn't exist
anymore.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:28.959
All you have to do is go and look at any place
where the law cannot be trusted.

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:32.650
You don't want to live anywhere like that.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:38.879
You want to live instead in a place where
your efforts are much less is a percentage

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:42.540
dominated by the job of just protecting yourself.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:50.230
Young people long for this, right, to use
their growing powers to make for themselves

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.359
a significant life.

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:57.110
That's what you want and you need good laws
for that.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.880
This idea that maybe in your mind that if
you don't like the place where you can go

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.370
you can move somewhere else.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:08.110
That's a fact by the way among the countries
that's still enjoy the rule of law, in the

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:15.620
other countries, not at all.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:20.200
The problem with government, the government
is the solution to a problem, right?

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:24.940
The necessary solution to a problem and that
is us.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.450
Lord knows what we might do without laws.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:34.730
We would be not unlikely to take each others
stuff, for example, but there's a problem

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.010
with government.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.370
That's us too.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:45.340
Madison wrote, "What is government but to
profound us to all commentaries on human nature.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.840
If men were angels, no government would be
needed.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:54.120
If angels were to govern men, neither internal
nor external controls on the government would

00:04:54.120 --> 00:05:00.620
be necessary."

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.320
Why should we listen to this old thing, right?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.130
Written for the time of the horse and buggy.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.070
It's actually true, George Washington had
wooden teeth.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.630
At least I think it's true.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:19.270
Serious people try to figure out what's right,
what fits.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:27.850
If there's a thing that is not susceptible
of change, we still are born in a certain

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:34.970
way, and then we age, and eventually we die
and that happens at a pace that's similar

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.240
for all of us.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:46.650
If we're going to remain human beings, then
my argument is we should strive to govern

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:51.040
ourselves in the way indicated by the constitution
of the United States.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.600
It is fit for things like us.

